;; Exact-once fire audit over DEMAND machinery (docs/stats.md): a linear
;; demand chain (count 3) -> (count 2) -> (count 1) -> (count 0), with a
;; prim-computed key so the supplementary transform engages.  Hand
;; verification: the step rule at :12 has exactly one satisfying body
;; assignment per demanded n>0 -- THREE instantiations total across all
;; its delta variants; its ask/sup rules likewise fire once per such n;
;; the base rule fires once ((count 0) demanded once); the driver rule at
;; :15 asks once and resumes once.  stats-tests.sh asserts the split.

demand (count int) int
rule (count 0 0)
rule (count n (+ 1 (count m))) <-- (> n 0) (= m (- n 1))

table (out int)
rule (out (count 3))
